{
  "updated_at": "2026-07-22 07:01 JST",
  "total": 50,
  "toyota_summary": "India has delayed its mandatory shift to E25 ethanol-blended fuel by at least a year, pushing back a major regulatory change that would have required automakers to redesign engines across their Indian lineup. The government will instead pursue a gradual phase-in approach. For the industry, this removes near-term pressure to retool production in one of the world's fastest-growing car markets, but signals that fuel infrastructure constraints remain a real barrier to rapid biofuel adoption.\n\nThe Trump administration revived Section 338 tariffs and imposed a 50 percent levy on roughly $20 billion in Canadian goods, marking a significant escalation in trade friction between the two countries. For automakers with integrated North American supply chains, this creates immediate cost pressure and forces recalculation of where to source parts and assemble vehicles across the region. Watch whether the tariff is applied to finished vehicles or remains limited to components and materials.",
